  "paraphrase": "For every function isquotprodprimefact from the rational numbers to propositions, if for every rational number q, isquotprodprimefact q is equivalent to the existence of natural numbers k and m, along with sequences a and b of prime numbers, such that q equals the product of the factorials of the elements of a divided by the product of the factorials of the elements of b, then for every non-negative rational number q, isquotprodprimefact q holds."
